HEAD subject=Cherry pick 3.6 (0701-0720) (#5649)

Key source findings
-------------------
- conf/nebula-storaged.conf.default:46: raft_heartbeat_interval_secs=30
- RaftPart.cpp:1411: polling delay = H*1000/3 + rand32(500)
- RaftPart.cpp:2041-2048: each idle leader polling cycle appends NORMAL empty log when !replicatingLogs_
- RaftPart.cpp:2051-2081: a separate Heartbeat RPC is also sent
- RaftPart.cpp:1912-1914: follower Heartbeat RPC path explicitly does not append logs
- Part.cpp:225-232: empty payload skips business operation only
- Part.cpp:349-358,403-410: the same empty log still writes per-partition commit key to RocksDB
- RocksEngine.cpp:124-134: commitBatchWrite calls db_->Write
- NebulaStore.cpp:395-421: one RocksEngine per space per data path
- conf/nebula-storaged.conf.default:102: write_buffer_size=67108864
- FileBasedWal.cpp:499: every log is pushed into AtomicLogBuffer
- AtomicLogBuffer.h:18,23-39: 64 records per Node; empty record logical size=16 bytes
- AtomicLogBuffer.cpp:91-119: capacity overflow marks old Node dirty, not immediate free
- AtomicLogBuffer.cpp:167-214: physical Node deletion happens in iterator release GC
- FileBasedWal.cpp:640-706: wal_ttl cleanup only deletes disk files and keeps at least two

