Timing cross-check
------------------
H=1 mean polling interval:
  floor(1000/3)+249.5 ms = 0.5825 sec

Theoretical write rate for one space with 20 local partitions:
  20 / 0.5825 = 34.33 entries/sec

Theoretical flush duration using observed 1281118-entry threshold:
  1281118 / 34.33 = 10.364 hours

Observed mean:
  10.3765 hours

Projected clean-heartbeat flush cycle:
  H=20 -> 5.127 days
  H=30 -> 7.599 days

AtomicLogBuffer timing cross-check
----------------------------------
Empty record logical size=16 bytes.
8 MiB / 16 = 524288 records before capacity pressure.
Six-dirty-node first GC point is approximately record 524610.

Projected first GC:
  H=1  -> 3.537 days
  H=20 -> 41.990 days
  H=30 -> 62.234 days

This does not match the first H=1 RocksDB drop at 10.4 hours or the production-scale multi-day drop.

